1
00:00:58,559 --> 00:00:59,393
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION

2
00:00:59,477 --> 00:01:00,978
CHILDREN WERE FILMED SAFELY
GEN AI WAS USED FOR SOME SCENES

3
00:01:03,939 --> 00:01:06,817
I'm thinking of quitting my job.

4
00:01:08,194 --> 00:01:09,195
Sorry?

5
00:01:09,904 --> 00:01:10,988
I'm going to quit.

6
00:01:11,864 --> 00:01:13,574
Why would you quit?

7
00:01:13,657 --> 00:01:14,742
It's cold.

8
00:01:14,825 --> 00:01:15,868
Let's talk inside.

9
00:01:31,801 --> 00:01:32,927
Warm up your hands first.

10
00:01:34,428 --> 00:01:35,679
So my hunch was right.

11
00:01:37,014 --> 00:01:38,724
You suddenly taking a day off,

12
00:01:39,433 --> 00:01:41,101
saying those weird things.

13
00:01:42,686 --> 00:01:44,438
I always seem to get caught by you.

14
00:01:44,522 --> 00:01:46,106
But still,

15
00:01:46,190 --> 00:01:48,442
I didn't think
you'd actually consider quitting.

16
00:01:48,526 --> 00:01:51,987
I wanted to clear my head first
then tell you before anyone else.

17
00:01:52,571 --> 00:01:54,907
If working together is the issue,

18
00:01:54,990 --> 00:01:56,992
I can just transfer
to the Development Team.

19
00:01:57,076 --> 00:01:59,954
You should stay where you are
and do the work you want to do.

20
00:02:00,037 --> 00:02:01,288
But what about you?

21
00:02:01,372 --> 00:02:02,331
I…

22
00:02:04,291 --> 00:02:06,168
don't have that anymore.

23
00:02:06,752 --> 00:02:07,586
Why not?

24
00:02:07,670 --> 00:02:10,673
I came this far determined to prove myself
through work, not politics.

25
00:02:11,674 --> 00:02:13,008
But at this rate,

26
00:02:13,092 --> 00:02:16,303
even if I get to the top,
I'll be forced to do things I hate.

27
00:02:17,638 --> 00:02:19,056
I don't want to do that.

28
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:22,935
But wouldn't it be the same
even if you moved to another company?

29
00:02:23,018 --> 00:02:23,936
I know.

30
00:02:24,436 --> 00:02:27,940
That's why I'm not jumping to another job.
I want to hit pause.

31
00:02:28,899 --> 00:02:30,901
I want to rediscover why
I chose this path,

32
00:02:30,985 --> 00:02:32,570
where my destination is,

33
00:02:32,653 --> 00:02:35,489
and what I really want to do.

34
00:02:37,783 --> 00:02:38,951
I'm so torn.

35
00:02:40,619 --> 00:02:42,413
As your girlfriend,

36
00:02:42,496 --> 00:02:44,623
I want to support your decision.

37
00:02:45,749 --> 00:02:48,502
But as a colleague,
I want to talk you out of it.

38
00:02:49,587 --> 00:02:50,838
It feels like a waste

39
00:02:52,006 --> 00:02:54,300
to throw away
everything you've worked for,

40
00:02:55,301 --> 00:02:56,927
and everything that would've followed.

41
00:02:57,011 --> 00:02:58,762
I don't regret walking away at all.

42
00:02:58,846 --> 00:03:00,973
I just want to be with you in peace

43
00:03:01,056 --> 00:03:02,850
and do work I actually want to do.

44
00:03:17,698 --> 00:03:18,782
Thank you.

45
00:03:18,866 --> 00:03:20,159
I'm the one who's grateful.

46
00:03:20,743 --> 00:03:23,829
Buying all this beef
for an old man's birthday.

47
00:03:25,623 --> 00:03:27,416
Happy birthday, sir.

48
00:03:30,336 --> 00:03:33,714
You must've been shocked
when he suddenly announced he's quitting.

49
00:03:35,716 --> 00:03:36,550
Yes.

50
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:40,971
To be honest,
my head is spinning right now.

51
00:03:42,306 --> 00:03:44,600
When Si-woo makes a decision,

52
00:03:45,768 --> 00:03:48,395
it's only after he's given it
everything he's got.

53
00:03:51,065 --> 00:03:52,983
Yes, I know that.

54
00:03:54,318 --> 00:03:56,487
And that's what upsets me.

55
00:03:58,238 --> 00:03:59,698
Why does he always

56
00:03:59,782 --> 00:04:02,868
try to struggle
through the hard times all by himself?

57
00:04:05,412 --> 00:04:07,247
I see why Si-woo fell for you.

58
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:12,169
Have you two been talking trash about me?

59
00:04:13,629 --> 00:04:14,755
Totally.

60
00:04:14,838 --> 00:04:18,550
I said I was worried if you'd still
be attractive even after you quit.

61
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:20,844
That feels like a threat.

62
00:04:23,222 --> 00:04:24,390
This is nice.

63
00:04:24,473 --> 00:04:26,558
You having someone to keep you in check.

64
00:04:28,018 --> 00:04:29,645
Yes, it really is.

65
00:04:39,029 --> 00:04:40,406
What are you thinking about?

66
00:04:40,990 --> 00:04:44,827
I'm just wondering
how much I'm allowed to interfere

67
00:04:45,536 --> 00:04:46,370
in your life.

68
00:04:46,453 --> 00:04:48,205
You're welcome to take full control.

69
00:04:50,582 --> 00:04:51,417
In that case,

70
00:04:52,209 --> 00:04:53,877
when are you submitting your resignation?

71
00:04:53,961 --> 00:04:55,462
What kind of company
do you want to go to?

72
00:04:55,546 --> 00:04:57,756
Do you want to start a business?
Got a business idea?

73
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:59,258
You're not going abroad, are you?

74
00:04:59,341 --> 00:05:01,260
Should I report to you
with a slide deck?

75
00:05:01,343 --> 00:05:03,262
Hey, I'm being serious right now.

76
00:05:03,345 --> 00:05:04,805
I'm submitting my resignation soon,

77
00:05:04,888 --> 00:05:07,266
and I'll figure out
the rest after that, one by one.

78
00:05:09,435 --> 00:05:11,311
Which means you literally have zero plan.

79
00:05:16,650 --> 00:05:17,860
Is this not the right way?

80
00:05:18,986 --> 00:05:20,904
Ms. Ji-yoon, could you check
the GPS for me?

81
00:05:21,905 --> 00:05:22,740
Sure.

82
00:05:23,532 --> 00:05:25,784
Looks like you took
the wrong turn at that fork earlier.

83
00:05:25,868 --> 00:05:27,786
We'll have to go a long way around.

84
00:05:29,204 --> 00:05:30,664
I got confused because it's dark.

85
00:05:30,748 --> 00:05:33,083
Well, I guess
you don't know everything after all.

86
00:05:33,167 --> 00:05:34,251
It's obvious

87
00:05:34,793 --> 00:05:36,670
I have to stay by your side
and coach you.

88
00:05:37,838 --> 00:05:38,922
I'm in your hands.

89
00:05:40,674 --> 00:05:42,676
I can't say I'm fully on board just yet,

90
00:05:43,552 --> 00:05:45,179
but I want to help you figure it out.

91
00:05:50,726 --> 00:05:51,560
Thank you.

92
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:57,399
Though I doubt our company
is going to let you walk away that easily.

93
00:06:04,656 --> 00:06:07,618
EPISODE 12

94
00:06:07,701 --> 00:06:11,830
NO MAP TO FOLLOW, STILL CLOCKING IN!

95
00:06:14,416 --> 00:06:15,959
What did you just say?

96
00:06:16,043 --> 00:06:17,169
I'm resigning.

97
00:06:17,252 --> 00:06:18,170
Si-woo!

98
00:06:18,253 --> 00:06:20,255
I wanted to tell you directly

99
00:06:20,339 --> 00:06:22,091
before handing in the paperwork.

100
00:06:22,174 --> 00:06:23,133
Are you doing this

101
00:06:23,759 --> 00:06:25,928
because Ms. Cha's special promotion
fell through?

102
00:06:26,011 --> 00:06:28,388
It's true I'm fed up
with the unfair evaluation system

103
00:06:28,472 --> 00:06:31,600
and disappointed by how conservative
this place is about new ideas.

104
00:06:32,184 --> 00:06:33,519
But through all of that,

105
00:06:33,602 --> 00:06:37,481
I finally realized that I'm someone
who doesn't belong in this organization.

106
00:06:37,564 --> 00:06:40,150
That's why I want us
to change this organization together!

107
00:06:40,234 --> 00:06:42,069
You cannot change it, President Han.

108
00:06:44,530 --> 00:06:45,781
Your position won't let you.

109
00:06:46,573 --> 00:06:47,574
I can't do it either.

110
00:06:50,035 --> 00:06:51,036
Think it over again.

111
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:55,666
Letting you go is a massive loss
not just for me, but to the whole company.

112
00:06:57,501 --> 00:06:58,669
I'll hand in my resignation.

113
00:06:58,752 --> 00:07:00,087
Absolutely not!

114
00:07:02,214 --> 00:07:03,132
Just wait.

115
00:07:12,516 --> 00:07:15,978
Everything discussed here today
is strictly confidential.

116
00:07:16,061 --> 00:07:16,895
Yes, ma'am.

117
00:07:17,771 --> 00:07:18,647
Yes, ma'am.

118
00:07:19,606 --> 00:07:21,567
Mr. Kang says he wants to quit.

119
00:07:23,318 --> 00:07:25,445
-But Mr. Kang is…
-Yes.

120
00:07:26,113 --> 00:07:28,365
He's a key asset
specially managed by the company.

121
00:07:30,534 --> 00:07:31,618
I'm sorry, ma'am.

122
00:07:31,702 --> 00:07:33,829
We missed the signs he wanted to leave.

123
00:07:34,913 --> 00:07:37,207
You look very surprised, Mr. Noh.

124
00:07:37,291 --> 00:07:40,669
It must be a headache finding out the guy
you desperately wanted to drag down

125
00:07:41,295 --> 00:07:42,713
is a key asset.

126
00:07:43,505 --> 00:07:47,176
I'll privately meet and convince him
with a bigger bonus or better role.

127
00:07:47,259 --> 00:07:48,594
That won't work.

128
00:07:50,929 --> 00:07:54,057
The moment
Mr. Kang's resignation is submitted,

129
00:07:54,141 --> 00:07:56,643
hold the approval process and just wait.

130
00:07:56,727 --> 00:07:59,688
Mr. Noh, you should
make the move in the meantime.

131
00:08:00,522 --> 00:08:01,398
Me?

132
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:04,151
You're the executive directly above him.

133
00:08:04,234 --> 00:08:05,068
Well, yes.

134
00:08:05,152 --> 00:08:07,988
If you become the executive
who lets a top performer slip away,

135
00:08:08,071 --> 00:08:10,282
your next performance review will suffer.

136
00:08:11,950 --> 00:08:12,993
Kang Si-woo.

137
00:08:13,076 --> 00:08:14,661
Keep him here at all costs.

138
00:08:15,871 --> 00:08:18,540
I will hold you accountable
for the outcome.

139
00:08:19,625 --> 00:08:20,584
Answer me.

140
00:08:23,337 --> 00:08:24,379
Yes, ma'am.

141
00:08:31,261 --> 00:08:32,971
What are you planning to do?

142
00:08:33,055 --> 00:08:34,973
First, we fix his work environment.

143
00:08:36,308 --> 00:08:39,728
Don't bother waiting for Manager Ko's
official disciplinary decision.

144
00:08:39,811 --> 00:08:40,979
Remove him immediately.

145
00:08:41,063 --> 00:08:41,939
Yes, sir.

146
00:09:09,633 --> 00:09:12,970
I bet you're thrilled to come to work
now that you won't see me for a while.

147
00:09:15,681 --> 00:09:16,807
"For a while."

148
00:09:19,851 --> 00:09:20,686
It won't be.

149
00:09:20,769 --> 00:09:21,645
Why?

150
00:09:22,312 --> 00:09:23,939
You think I'm never coming back?

151
00:09:24,022 --> 00:09:25,315
Just you wait.

152
00:09:25,399 --> 00:09:28,151
I'll make sure to return
and make you leave the company.

153
00:09:29,695 --> 00:09:31,363
Sure. I can't wait.

154
00:09:34,157 --> 00:09:37,369
You've been an arrogant brat
from day one, and even now.

155
00:09:37,452 --> 00:09:39,997
My life started going wrong
ever since I met you!

156
00:09:43,542 --> 00:09:46,003
I would've been different
if I hadn't had you as my boss.

157
00:09:47,045 --> 00:09:47,879
What?

158
00:09:47,963 --> 00:09:51,216
It seems you don't have
much luck with bosses either.

159
00:10:00,559 --> 00:10:01,768
Go ahead and take this one.

160
00:10:01,852 --> 00:10:03,770
I'll catch the next.

161
00:10:04,646 --> 00:10:06,481
-Doors are closing.
-Hey! You little…

162
00:10:07,691 --> 00:10:08,734
An accountant?

163
00:10:09,735 --> 00:10:11,194
How does he look?

164
00:10:12,029 --> 00:10:13,447
No, it's just…

165
00:10:13,530 --> 00:10:16,742
Ji-yoon cares more
about a guy's looks than his job.

166
00:10:16,825 --> 00:10:18,535
Right, okay.

167
00:10:19,911 --> 00:10:22,414
Then I guess I'll ask her about it.

168
00:10:23,415 --> 00:10:24,499
Okay.

169
00:10:33,342 --> 00:10:34,676
What's gotten into you?

170
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:36,386
Isn't this what you wanted?

171
00:10:41,975 --> 00:10:42,809
It's so sour.

172
00:10:43,477 --> 00:10:44,895
Just leave Ji-yoon alone.

173
00:10:45,479 --> 00:10:47,981
I don't enjoy
getting nagged by her either.

174
00:10:49,066 --> 00:10:49,900
But people

175
00:10:50,567 --> 00:10:53,362
won't stop pestering me
because she works at SAEUM.

176
00:10:53,987 --> 00:10:55,238
What about your regular?

177
00:10:55,322 --> 00:10:57,199
I told you to play matchmaker.
What happened?

178
00:10:57,282 --> 00:10:58,950
Matchmaker? Come on.

179
00:10:59,034 --> 00:11:00,535
It'll work out if it's meant to be.

180
00:11:00,619 --> 00:11:03,330
How would they magically cross paths
in a company that big?

181
00:11:04,956 --> 00:11:06,416
Why? Is something wrong with him?

182
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:08,835
What? Don't jump to conclusions like that.

183
00:11:08,919 --> 00:11:11,630
Do you really think
I'd grab drinks with a bad guy?

184
00:11:11,713 --> 00:11:13,006
That's exactly my point.

185
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:15,634
Who'd hang out with a boring guy like you?

186
00:11:15,717 --> 00:11:17,844
-Hey, now.
-What's his title?

187
00:11:17,928 --> 00:11:20,013
Does he live alone?
Are his parents both around?

188
00:11:21,973 --> 00:11:24,017
Giving me the silent treatment again.

189
00:11:24,101 --> 00:11:26,686
If you don't want to do it yourself,
give me his number.

190
00:11:37,197 --> 00:11:38,365
Hey, that's my phone.

191
00:11:38,448 --> 00:11:40,200
What's yours is still mine.

192
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:43,954
Where are you going?

193
00:11:44,704 --> 00:11:46,206
We have to go to the divorce lawyer.

194
00:11:46,289 --> 00:11:47,249
I'm not going.

195
00:11:50,752 --> 00:11:53,463
Everyone, great job on the Home-AI launch.

196
00:11:55,006 --> 00:11:58,718
The Sales and Marketing Teams
will take over the rest from now on.

197
00:11:58,802 --> 00:12:00,720
So what project will we work on next?

198
00:12:00,804 --> 00:12:02,305
As of today, this task force…

199
00:12:02,389 --> 00:12:04,474
Drumroll, please!

200
00:12:05,142 --> 00:12:06,101
…is disbanded.

201
00:12:08,019 --> 00:12:09,813
-Pardon?
-Why, all of a sudden?

202
00:12:11,022 --> 00:12:13,233
I'll do everything I can
to make sure you all move

203
00:12:13,984 --> 00:12:15,152
to the teams you want.

204
00:12:15,819 --> 00:12:16,862
Mr. Kang.

205
00:12:18,947 --> 00:12:21,700
I'd like to head back
to Product Planning Team 1.

206
00:12:21,783 --> 00:12:22,617
Sure.

207
00:12:23,535 --> 00:12:25,787
Let me know
once you two make up your minds.

208
00:12:25,871 --> 00:12:28,790
And here I was,
thinking of ideas for the next project.

209
00:12:29,624 --> 00:12:31,084
Do that back in your teams.

210
00:12:31,168 --> 00:12:32,627
What can I do there?

211
00:12:33,670 --> 00:12:36,590
They'll tell me to stick to the old way
even if I pitch a new idea.

212
00:12:37,048 --> 00:12:39,676
I can't work like I do now
under any other boss.

213
00:12:40,594 --> 00:12:44,014
Look, what if we found
a new project to work on?

214
00:12:44,097 --> 00:12:47,142
We'll pull all-nighters to find something
even the higher-ups can't refuse.

215
00:12:47,225 --> 00:12:48,101
So please…

216
00:12:49,519 --> 00:12:52,981
Can't you just stay on
as our boss, Mr. Kang?

217
00:12:57,777 --> 00:13:01,114
You three are the heroes
who made Home-AI a success.

218
00:13:02,324 --> 00:13:04,910
No matter who your boss is
or what team you're on,

219
00:13:04,993 --> 00:13:06,870
keep working with your heads held high.

220
00:13:06,953 --> 00:13:08,705
You've earned the right to do that.

221
00:13:18,465 --> 00:13:19,758
Go have a nice lunch

222
00:13:19,841 --> 00:13:21,134
with this today.

223
00:13:22,719 --> 00:13:23,887
What about you, sir?

224
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:25,347
Something urgent came up.

225
00:13:25,430 --> 00:13:26,473
I'll join next time.

226
00:13:31,686 --> 00:13:33,146
What's going on here?

227
00:13:33,730 --> 00:13:35,857
The task force was always just temporary.

228
00:13:35,941 --> 00:13:39,110
It's natural to get dissolved
now that the project is over.

229
00:13:39,194 --> 00:13:41,363
And what about Mr. Kang? Where's he going?

230
00:13:41,446 --> 00:13:43,949
Oh, is he taking over Mr. Ko's position?

231
00:13:44,032 --> 00:13:45,784
Is that why you're going there too?

232
00:13:45,867 --> 00:13:48,620
No, he's not going anywhere for a while.

233
00:13:49,204 --> 00:13:50,497
What's that supposed to mean?

234
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:52,123
He says nothing is decided yet.

235
00:13:55,961 --> 00:13:57,337
You two grab lunch without me.

236
00:14:00,549 --> 00:14:01,675
What? Ji-yoon.

237
00:14:10,850 --> 00:14:12,227
Mom,

238
00:14:12,310 --> 00:14:14,479
this is so rude to the other person.

239
00:14:14,563 --> 00:14:16,940
I keep telling you I don't want to. Why…

240
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:25,448
That's the guy you set me up
for a blind date?

241
00:14:25,532 --> 00:14:27,659
He seemed like a great guy.

242
00:14:27,742 --> 00:14:31,037
He works at SAEUM too,
so you can meet even when you're busy.

243
00:14:31,121 --> 00:14:32,497
Mom, let me call you back.

244
00:14:38,086 --> 00:14:39,546
So this was your urgent thing?

245
00:14:42,841 --> 00:14:44,342
Did your mother call you here too?

246
00:14:44,926 --> 00:14:48,388
Wow, so you came out here
to meet my mom, did you?

247
00:14:48,471 --> 00:14:50,390
Yet you didn't mention a word to me.

248
00:14:50,473 --> 00:14:52,309
I didn't know why she wanted to see me.

249
00:14:52,392 --> 00:14:54,894
Even so,
you should've given me a heads-up.

250
00:14:54,978 --> 00:14:56,688
I was completely clueless.

251
00:15:02,569 --> 00:15:04,654
Wait, is this a lunch blind date?

252
00:15:08,950 --> 00:15:12,412
Wow, going on a blind date
behind my back, are we?

253
00:15:12,495 --> 00:15:16,833
No. I only came to politely turn him down.

254
00:15:22,005 --> 00:15:25,383
My mom must've
really taken a liking to you.

255
00:15:25,467 --> 00:15:26,968
Well, that's a relief.

256
00:15:28,136 --> 00:15:29,095
But what do we do now?

257
00:15:29,679 --> 00:15:33,141
I guess we should tell her the truth
before she catches us, right?

258
00:15:34,559 --> 00:15:35,727
Yes.

259
00:15:43,485 --> 00:15:44,527
Hello.

260
00:15:45,528 --> 00:15:46,738
Can I help you?

261
00:15:48,448 --> 00:15:51,743
Is Jae-in around by any chance?

262
00:15:51,826 --> 00:15:53,370
Oh, he just stepped out.

263
00:15:55,246 --> 00:15:57,457
Wait. You're Ms. Yoon, right?

264
00:15:57,540 --> 00:15:58,875
Do you know who I am?

265
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:01,961
Of course. Jae-in never stops
bragging about his girlfriend.

266
00:16:04,756 --> 00:16:05,757
He'll be back soon.

267
00:16:09,177 --> 00:16:10,136
Hey, I forgot my…

268
00:16:19,521 --> 00:16:20,355
Why are you here?

269
00:16:22,774 --> 00:16:24,109
Because I can't let you go.

270
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:27,779
I know exactly how selfish I'm being.

271
00:16:28,863 --> 00:16:31,991
I don't want to lose you,
and I still want to go to Senegal.

272
00:16:34,369 --> 00:16:37,831
But I really don't want
to give up on either.

273
00:16:47,173 --> 00:16:50,009
I grew up moving from country to country
because of my dad's job.

274
00:16:51,136 --> 00:16:54,848
People envied me,
but I never had any friends.

275
00:16:54,931 --> 00:16:56,850
Every time I got
close to someone, we moved.

276
00:16:58,184 --> 00:16:59,519
I moved back to Korea

277
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:01,604
because I insisted on coming
when I turned 20

278
00:17:02,522 --> 00:17:03,815
even if I had to come alone.

279
00:17:05,859 --> 00:17:08,445
Now, I finally have people
I can call real friends

280
00:17:09,612 --> 00:17:11,072
and a lot of things I want to do.

281
00:17:13,241 --> 00:17:14,492
So right now…

282
00:17:17,662 --> 00:17:19,289
I can't follow you, No-ah.

283
00:17:21,791 --> 00:17:23,376
I can't handle long-distance either.

284
00:17:25,462 --> 00:17:26,963
I'm scared too.

285
00:17:27,881 --> 00:17:28,715
But…

286
00:17:30,341 --> 00:17:32,510
I'm scared of losing you even more.

287
00:17:41,102 --> 00:17:42,020
I'm sorry.

288
00:17:44,606 --> 00:17:45,982
I don't think I can do it.

289
00:17:51,821 --> 00:17:52,739
No.

290
00:17:54,324 --> 00:17:55,867
I'm the one who's sorry.

291
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:16,429
Weren't you the one
dying to see her every second?

292
00:18:16,513 --> 00:18:18,139
I still am.

293
00:18:18,223 --> 00:18:19,432
That's why I'm doing this.

294
00:18:20,475 --> 00:18:22,435
I don't know the full story,

295
00:18:22,519 --> 00:18:25,396
but hey, the stupidest thing you can do

296
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:27,982
is force an end to something
that isn't over yet.

297
00:18:29,984 --> 00:18:31,277
But I can see how it'll end.

298
00:18:31,361 --> 00:18:32,862
Look at this kid, so cocky.

299
00:18:33,655 --> 00:18:36,241
How can you know the end
if you haven't even been there?

300
00:18:46,918 --> 00:18:48,002
Do you like it?

301
00:18:49,212 --> 00:18:51,714
Yeah, I do, but… Gosh.

302
00:18:52,215 --> 00:18:54,884
I don't know how often
I'll wear something this pricey.

303
00:18:54,968 --> 00:18:56,469
Just wear it all the time.

304
00:18:56,553 --> 00:18:58,471
Wear it when you meet your friends,

305
00:18:59,013 --> 00:19:00,557
or when you go on a date with Dad.

306
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:02,559
A date with your dad? Good grief.

307
00:19:02,642 --> 00:19:04,310
I already see him at home all day.

308
00:19:04,978 --> 00:19:08,022
It seems like
he's trying really hard, though.

309
00:19:08,690 --> 00:19:10,942
Do you still want
to graduate from marriage?

310
00:19:11,025 --> 00:19:13,361
Being nice for a bit
doesn't erase years of resentment.

311
00:19:14,279 --> 00:19:15,822
I need to watch and see a bit more.

312
00:19:16,322 --> 00:19:17,156
So you're saying

313
00:19:18,116 --> 00:19:20,034
there's a glimmer of hope for him?

314
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:23,830
Wait, why are you so quiet?

315
00:19:23,913 --> 00:19:27,584
I expected you to throw a massive fit,
but you're buying me clothes and food.

316
00:19:29,127 --> 00:19:30,420
Did you actually like him?

317
00:19:32,755 --> 00:19:33,631
Yeah.

318
00:19:35,633 --> 00:19:36,968
I like him a lot.

319
00:19:37,051 --> 00:19:38,553
See? I told you!

320
00:19:39,053 --> 00:19:40,972
He totally won me over too!

321
00:19:41,556 --> 00:19:43,641
So did you agree to start seeing him?

322
00:19:45,143 --> 00:19:46,227
The truth is,

323
00:19:47,061 --> 00:19:49,355
we were already seeing each other.

324
00:19:50,565 --> 00:19:53,610
Mr. Kang is actually my boss.

325
00:19:54,444 --> 00:19:55,486
What?

326
00:19:55,570 --> 00:19:58,323
I liked him as a colleague at first,

327
00:19:59,866 --> 00:20:01,868
then I liked him as a man,

328
00:20:02,577 --> 00:20:05,330
and now I'm in love with him.

329
00:20:05,997 --> 00:20:08,166
You're already a couple?

330
00:20:09,042 --> 00:20:09,876
Yeah.

331
00:20:09,959 --> 00:20:10,960
My goodness!

332
00:20:12,337 --> 00:20:13,546
And here I was,

333
00:20:13,630 --> 00:20:15,632
playing matchmaker for you like a fool.

334
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:18,593
Wait, did your dad
not know about this either?

335
00:20:19,177 --> 00:20:22,263
He actually caught us together
a little while ago,

336
00:20:23,890 --> 00:20:26,392
but he probably couldn't
bring himself to tell you.

337
00:20:26,476 --> 00:20:27,560
Why not?

338
00:20:27,644 --> 00:20:30,480
Why couldn't he say
two of his favorite people are dating?

339
00:20:31,356 --> 00:20:32,357
He's…

340
00:20:35,109 --> 00:20:36,611
been through a divorce.

341
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:40,156
What?

342
00:20:59,634 --> 00:21:01,636
It was a hurdle
you had to cross eventually.

343
00:21:02,887 --> 00:21:04,180
Trust Ji-yoon and just wait.

344
00:21:04,931 --> 00:21:06,474
Are you rooting for me?

345
00:21:06,557 --> 00:21:07,934
Why would I root for you?

346
00:21:09,686 --> 00:21:10,895
I'm rooting for my daughter.

347
00:21:12,855 --> 00:21:14,857
I'll say it again,

348
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:17,402
I'm on my wife's side, no matter what,

349
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:19,445
even if that upsets you.

350
00:21:19,529 --> 00:21:21,614
That's fine.
I have someone on my side too.

351
00:21:21,698 --> 00:21:22,824
She's my daughter!

352
00:21:26,577 --> 00:21:29,372
What would you do
if my wife doesn't approve of you?

353
00:21:29,956 --> 00:21:30,915
I'll have to wait

354
00:21:31,624 --> 00:21:33,292
until Mother warms up to me.

355
00:21:36,170 --> 00:21:37,130
Hang on.

356
00:21:38,131 --> 00:21:40,717
How come she's "Mother"
and I'm just "sir"?

357
00:21:42,260 --> 00:21:43,886
Then please help me out,

358
00:21:43,970 --> 00:21:45,346
Father.

359
00:21:48,266 --> 00:21:50,184
As if I stand a chance against my wife.

360
00:21:54,772 --> 00:21:57,650
How could you just storm out
without even hearing the whole story?

361
00:21:57,734 --> 00:21:59,819
I said no.
What else is there to talk about?

362
00:21:59,902 --> 00:22:01,029
Why not?

363
00:22:01,112 --> 00:22:03,072
You wanted to graduate from marriage too.

364
00:22:03,156 --> 00:22:04,866
You'd understand him more than anyone.

365
00:22:04,949 --> 00:22:06,784
Yeah, I'm dying to graduate from marriage!

366
00:22:08,036 --> 00:22:10,038
Because I endured all those years.

367
00:22:11,831 --> 00:22:14,917
Most couples go through a phase
of wanting to break up.

368
00:22:15,001 --> 00:22:17,879
But everyone just sticks it out
and works through it.

369
00:22:18,880 --> 00:22:19,714
But…

370
00:22:20,256 --> 00:22:21,966
He got a divorce in less than a year?

371
00:22:23,593 --> 00:22:25,720
How can you trust someone
who gives up that easily?

372
00:22:25,803 --> 00:22:29,682
But working through it is something
you're supposed to do together.

373
00:22:29,766 --> 00:22:32,810
Mr. Kang never even got that chance.

374
00:22:32,894 --> 00:22:35,605
Then he shouldn't have gotten married
in the first place!

375
00:22:35,688 --> 00:22:36,564
Mom.

376
00:22:39,025 --> 00:22:41,402
Call me shallow all you want,
but I can't help it.

377
00:22:42,653 --> 00:22:45,573
I want my daughter
to go down an easy path,

378
00:22:46,407 --> 00:22:49,035
not tripping and falling over stones.

379
00:22:49,911 --> 00:22:51,079
I can't approve of this.

380
00:23:07,095 --> 00:23:08,471
We knew this would happen.

381
00:23:08,888 --> 00:23:12,308
Still, I didn't think
she'd be so strongly against it.

382
00:23:13,017 --> 00:23:14,143
I understand her, though.

383
00:23:14,560 --> 00:23:16,896
I'm hardly ideal from her perspective.

384
00:23:18,022 --> 00:23:20,066
Yes, I know it's
because she cares about me.

385
00:23:23,236 --> 00:23:24,195
It's fine.

386
00:23:25,071 --> 00:23:28,407
I'm going to keep seeing you
no matter what my mom says.

387
00:23:29,575 --> 00:23:31,119
So don't let it get to you either.

388
00:23:31,202 --> 00:23:33,412
We're in this
to get married one day anyway.

389
00:23:34,288 --> 00:23:36,791
Then we need to get her blessing
even if it takes time.

390
00:23:38,209 --> 00:23:39,168
But how?

391
00:23:41,462 --> 00:23:44,006
You do things your way.
I'll do things my way.

392
00:23:44,757 --> 00:23:45,800
One step at a time.

393
00:23:48,219 --> 00:23:50,471
-Are you Ms. Nam Hye-gyeong?
-Yes, that's me.

394
00:23:50,555 --> 00:23:51,430
Here's your package.

395
00:23:51,514 --> 00:23:52,765
FRAGILE
PREMIUM RED GINSENG

396
00:23:54,183 --> 00:23:55,101
Red ginseng?

397
00:23:55,184 --> 00:23:57,019
Who sent this?

398
00:23:58,813 --> 00:24:00,982
-It's from an anonymous sender.
-Okay.

399
00:24:01,607 --> 00:24:02,817
Thank you.

400
00:24:16,873 --> 00:24:18,583
What brings you here so early?

401
00:24:19,250 --> 00:24:22,044
What do you mean? I'm just working out.

402
00:24:22,670 --> 00:24:25,131
We should do it together.
You're a key asset, after all.

403
00:24:29,302 --> 00:24:30,386
Do you play golf at all?

404
00:24:31,429 --> 00:24:32,597
I don't care for golf.

405
00:24:33,598 --> 00:24:34,557
That won't do.

406
00:24:35,183 --> 00:24:37,393
You have to pick it up
if you want to make executive.

407
00:24:38,352 --> 00:24:41,522
I have a private coach, you know.
We could learn toge--

408
00:24:44,609 --> 00:24:45,610
Oh, gosh.

409
00:24:45,693 --> 00:24:48,487
We won't go golfing together.
Please tell me what you want.

410
00:24:48,571 --> 00:24:50,448
Are you serious about quitting?

411
00:24:51,115 --> 00:24:52,241
Yes.

412
00:24:52,325 --> 00:24:54,660
Look, I can see where you're coming from,

413
00:24:54,744 --> 00:24:57,705
but at least think of President Han.
She thinks the world of you.

414
00:24:59,874 --> 00:25:03,085
It's pretty funny hearing you
express concern for President Han.

415
00:25:04,921 --> 00:25:05,922
Don't worry.

416
00:25:06,005 --> 00:25:08,549
She'll be perfectly fine even without me.

417
00:25:12,970 --> 00:25:13,846
Hey, Kang Si-woo!

418
00:25:15,723 --> 00:25:17,141
Oh, come on.

419
00:25:19,769 --> 00:25:21,354
Since we don't have a team lead,

420
00:25:21,437 --> 00:25:24,148
I'll temporarily be taking over
as acting lead.

421
00:25:24,982 --> 00:25:27,735
Everyone can just keep doing
what they were doing.

422
00:25:27,818 --> 00:25:28,778
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

423
00:25:29,320 --> 00:25:30,529
Oh, please.

424
00:25:32,448 --> 00:25:35,493
Ms. Yoon, please hand over your work
to Ms. Cha before you leave.

425
00:25:35,576 --> 00:25:36,410
Yes, sir.

426
00:25:36,494 --> 00:25:38,079
A new hire arrives today.

427
00:25:38,162 --> 00:25:39,664
Can someone be his mentor?

428
00:25:45,795 --> 00:25:46,754
Anyone?

429
00:25:48,464 --> 00:25:50,258
Oh, look. Here he comes.

430
00:26:06,941 --> 00:26:07,775
Hello!

431
00:26:08,359 --> 00:26:09,986
I'm the rookie, Song Min-gyu.

432
00:26:12,655 --> 00:26:13,990
I'll do it.

433
00:26:20,746 --> 00:26:21,580
Thank you.

434
00:26:30,298 --> 00:26:32,049
Ms. Shin went back to her old team.

435
00:26:32,591 --> 00:26:34,593
Have you not decided yet?

436
00:26:35,261 --> 00:26:36,304
Well, I…

437
00:26:36,887 --> 00:26:39,807
I wanted to decide
after seeing where you go first.

438
00:26:40,599 --> 00:26:41,684
Why? To follow me?

439
00:26:42,310 --> 00:26:43,394
Yes.

440
00:26:47,064 --> 00:26:48,232
I'm going to resign.

441
00:26:48,316 --> 00:26:49,608
Right.

442
00:26:50,735 --> 00:26:51,902
Pardon?

443
00:26:51,986 --> 00:26:53,863
So don't wait on me
and make your decision.

444
00:26:54,572 --> 00:26:55,448
But why?

445
00:26:55,531 --> 00:26:58,075
I want to look for work
that suits me better.

446
00:26:58,909 --> 00:27:00,911
I hope you take
this chance to do the same.

447
00:27:01,620 --> 00:27:04,415
But working under you
is what suits me the best.

448
00:27:08,127 --> 00:27:09,211
What about the Development Team?

449
00:27:09,295 --> 00:27:12,048
You seemed more excited doing
that work than planning work.

450
00:27:12,131 --> 00:27:13,382
That's not wrong,

451
00:27:13,466 --> 00:27:15,468
but going to Development now is a bit…

452
00:27:15,551 --> 00:27:17,762
Everyone's been raving
about your washer-dryer.

453
00:27:18,721 --> 00:27:21,724
No one would question it
if you transferred there.

454
00:27:22,892 --> 00:27:23,768
Okay.

455
00:27:24,685 --> 00:27:25,978
I'll do it, then.

456
00:27:26,062 --> 00:27:28,314
I'll speak to their team lead.

457
00:27:28,939 --> 00:27:30,024
In return,

458
00:27:30,107 --> 00:27:32,818
please keep my resignation
under wraps for now.

459
00:27:34,737 --> 00:27:36,238
It's a real shame.

460
00:27:36,322 --> 00:27:38,407
Though I'm sure you're moving on
to better things.

461
00:27:40,368 --> 00:27:41,619
Right.

462
00:27:42,661 --> 00:27:44,747
I'll go somewhere better.

463
00:27:49,460 --> 00:27:50,503
I know, right?

464
00:27:51,087 --> 00:27:52,421
Mr. Kang!

465
00:27:54,507 --> 00:27:55,841
This is our new hire.

466
00:27:55,925 --> 00:27:57,510
This is Manager Kang Si-woo.

467
00:27:59,053 --> 00:28:01,138
Hello. My name is Song Min-gyu.

468
00:28:02,181 --> 00:28:03,015
Okay.

469
00:28:04,308 --> 00:28:06,102
I think you came to the wrong place.

470
00:28:06,185 --> 00:28:08,562
You're too handsome to work
at an electronics company.

471
00:28:11,023 --> 00:28:13,359
A lot of people do tell me
I look like a movie star.

472
00:28:14,652 --> 00:28:16,112
Wow, the confident type.

473
00:28:17,113 --> 00:28:19,323
What can I get you, Min-gyu?

474
00:28:19,407 --> 00:28:20,658
Do you like instant coffee?

475
00:28:21,784 --> 00:28:24,495
If your mentor offers you
instant coffee, you should say no.

476
00:28:26,705 --> 00:28:27,623
Just a moment.

477
00:28:28,999 --> 00:28:31,043
"Say no to instant coffee."

478
00:28:31,127 --> 00:28:32,211
CHECKLIST
NO TO INSTANT COFFEE

479
00:28:32,962 --> 00:28:35,089
-Understood, sir.
-Also say no when she tempts you

480
00:28:35,172 --> 00:28:36,090
with chicken and beer.

481
00:28:37,425 --> 00:28:39,427
"Say no to chicken and beer."

482
00:28:40,010 --> 00:28:41,011
And for the record,

483
00:28:41,095 --> 00:28:43,305
Ms. Cha already has a boyfriend.

484
00:28:44,306 --> 00:28:46,851
"Already has a boyfriend…"

485
00:28:52,565 --> 00:28:53,524
Right.

486
00:28:55,025 --> 00:28:55,901
I'll take note.

487
00:28:57,319 --> 00:28:58,237
You're lucky

488
00:28:58,320 --> 00:29:00,698
to land a great superior from day one.

489
00:29:05,286 --> 00:29:06,120
Yes.

490
00:29:14,086 --> 00:29:15,713
What is it this time?

491
00:29:15,796 --> 00:29:17,423
It says health supplements.

492
00:29:32,480 --> 00:29:33,397
Oh, geez.

493
00:29:33,481 --> 00:29:36,317
PREMIUM MULTIVITAMIN FOR WOMEN
RED GINSENG

494
00:29:36,400 --> 00:29:38,736
TO: NAM HYE-GYEONG

495
00:29:58,506 --> 00:30:00,341
If you don't respect me,

496
00:30:00,424 --> 00:30:02,259
I won't respect you either.

497
00:30:03,886 --> 00:30:04,720
Okay.

498
00:30:05,638 --> 00:30:07,306
Even in a relationship,

499
00:30:07,389 --> 00:30:09,058
I'm going to put myself first.

500
00:30:09,934 --> 00:30:10,768
Okay.

501
00:30:10,851 --> 00:30:12,603
If your love fades away…

502
00:30:13,187 --> 00:30:14,855
I won't forgive it and just leave.

503
00:30:16,607 --> 00:30:17,483
Okay.

504
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:19,860
That's how I'm going to love you.

505
00:30:21,403 --> 00:30:22,571
I want you to do the same.

506
00:30:25,449 --> 00:30:26,283
Okay.

507
00:30:26,367 --> 00:30:27,743
It's the first time

508
00:30:27,826 --> 00:30:29,620
I've been recognized at work
for my own effort.

509
00:30:30,496 --> 00:30:32,164
If I choose to be with you,

510
00:30:32,248 --> 00:30:34,583
I want it to be
as a better version of myself.

511
00:30:35,417 --> 00:30:38,712
Before being Lee Jae-in's girlfriend,

512
00:30:40,339 --> 00:30:41,549
I want to be Yoon No-ah first.

513
00:30:43,050 --> 00:30:44,593
I'm scared too.

514
00:30:45,344 --> 00:30:48,806
But I'm scared of losing you even more.

515
00:31:07,533 --> 00:31:08,367
No-ah.

516
00:31:10,327 --> 00:31:12,580
Kim Goo-won? What are you doing here?

517
00:31:16,125 --> 00:31:18,502
I can't take it anymore.
Let's get back together.

518
00:31:19,628 --> 00:31:21,171
What the heck are you doing?

519
00:31:23,465 --> 00:31:25,509
I heard you're still with that young kid.

520
00:31:26,635 --> 00:31:30,264
Snap out of it, No-ah.
Why are you destroying your life over me?

521
00:31:31,265 --> 00:31:32,808
Did you fight with your girlfriend?

522
00:31:33,309 --> 00:31:34,893
I'll end things with Da-eun soon.

523
00:31:34,977 --> 00:31:36,353
You haven't changed at all.

524
00:31:37,813 --> 00:31:38,814
You piece of trash.

525
00:31:41,525 --> 00:31:44,069
Look at yourself.
Do you realize how much you've changed?

526
00:31:45,029 --> 00:31:46,614
You're not the No-ah I used to know.

527
00:31:46,697 --> 00:31:48,657
Yeah, I've changed!

528
00:31:49,158 --> 00:31:52,494
I've become more selfish and brave
than you could ever imagine.

529
00:31:54,121 --> 00:31:55,956
So please, get the hell out of my life.

530
00:31:57,207 --> 00:31:59,835
Listen, No-ah. You need me.

531
00:32:01,420 --> 00:32:02,421
Let go.

532
00:32:03,547 --> 00:32:04,673
I said let go.

533
00:32:05,215 --> 00:32:06,050
Let go!

534
00:32:09,094 --> 00:32:10,179
She told you to let go.

535
00:32:12,181 --> 00:32:13,307
Why don't you get lost

536
00:32:13,390 --> 00:32:14,933
and stop bugging No-ah?

537
00:32:15,017 --> 00:32:16,977
I'm not bugging her. I love her.

538
00:32:17,686 --> 00:32:19,021
Love, my ass.

539
00:32:19,104 --> 00:32:21,649
You don't know much about No-ah.
And you say you love her?

540
00:32:21,732 --> 00:32:23,192
I know better than you

541
00:32:24,068 --> 00:32:25,986
what an amazing woman No-ah is.

542
00:32:32,409 --> 00:32:34,870
Listen carefully, Kim Goo-won.

543
00:32:34,953 --> 00:32:36,997
Jae-in is the one I love.

544
00:32:38,040 --> 00:32:39,583
So don't ever show your face again.

545
00:32:39,667 --> 00:32:41,168
I'm calling the cops if you do.

546
00:32:43,003 --> 00:32:45,589
Don't come crawling back to me crying
when this goes south.

547
00:32:59,520 --> 00:33:00,396
Jae-in.

548
00:33:03,190 --> 00:33:04,358
I can't promise

549
00:33:04,942 --> 00:33:06,610
I'll wait for you until you get back.

550
00:33:08,404 --> 00:33:09,571
Are you okay with that?

551
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:14,034
Yeah.

552
00:33:14,410 --> 00:33:15,661
If either of us gets fed up,

553
00:33:16,245 --> 00:33:18,163
we'll call it quits then and there.

554
00:33:19,915 --> 00:33:20,874
Is that okay?

555
00:33:22,459 --> 00:33:23,419
Yeah.

556
00:33:23,502 --> 00:33:25,379
But I know for a fact I won't get fed up.

557
00:33:27,631 --> 00:33:28,590
I told you before.

558
00:33:29,508 --> 00:33:31,510
Love isn't about enduring
and forcing effort.

559
00:33:31,593 --> 00:33:33,053
I won't hold back or endure.

560
00:33:33,137 --> 00:33:36,473
I'm going to video call you every day
and write letters every day

561
00:33:36,557 --> 00:33:38,183
and fly back at least twice a year.

562
00:33:38,267 --> 00:33:40,811
I'll come see you
even if we have to meet halfway

563
00:33:40,894 --> 00:33:41,979
in some random country.

564
00:33:52,364 --> 00:33:54,491
I'll have to see you more
before you leave.

565
00:33:57,244 --> 00:33:58,078
Yeah.

566
00:34:09,882 --> 00:34:11,091
What are you doing here?

567
00:34:14,344 --> 00:34:15,554
Hello, Mother.

568
00:34:15,637 --> 00:34:17,431
Don't call me that, it's uncomfortable.

569
00:34:19,725 --> 00:34:20,809
I asked what you're doing.

570
00:34:20,893 --> 00:34:23,353
Whenever I need to clear my head,

571
00:34:23,437 --> 00:34:25,272
I come help out around the store.

572
00:34:27,941 --> 00:34:29,568
Don't people usually send

573
00:34:29,651 --> 00:34:32,488
flowers or fruit baskets
when they try to win someone over?

574
00:34:33,238 --> 00:34:36,241
Why did you only send supplements?
You're treating me like an old lady.

575
00:34:36,325 --> 00:34:38,744
I don't like seeing
the people I care about get sick.

576
00:34:42,998 --> 00:34:44,875
Do you give Ji-yoon gifts like that too?

577
00:34:45,834 --> 00:34:46,668
Yes.

578
00:34:46,752 --> 00:34:49,963
You men truly have no clue
what women actually want.

579
00:34:52,049 --> 00:34:53,842
How long did you intend to send me those?

580
00:34:53,926 --> 00:34:55,636
Until you called and told me to stop.

581
00:34:57,012 --> 00:34:59,264
I didn't want to show up
and make you uncomfortable,

582
00:34:59,348 --> 00:35:00,182
so I waited.

583
00:35:01,391 --> 00:35:03,143
The ship might sail while you wait.

584
00:35:04,645 --> 00:35:06,980
Anyway, then try fixing this.
It won't turn on.

585
00:35:08,023 --> 00:35:08,857
Sure.

586
00:35:26,333 --> 00:35:28,293
That back looks awfully familiar.

587
00:35:32,631 --> 00:35:34,174
What is it you like about Ji-yoon?

588
00:35:41,056 --> 00:35:44,643
I admire her confidence that stems
from her deep sense of responsibility.

589
00:35:46,478 --> 00:35:48,939
She always finds solutions
no one else can think of,

590
00:35:49,022 --> 00:35:50,190
and once she sets a goal,

591
00:35:50,274 --> 00:35:52,317
she gives it her all
until she's satisfied.

592
00:35:53,402 --> 00:35:54,903
And unlike me,

593
00:35:55,737 --> 00:35:58,365
she knows how to open up
and share her feelings.

594
00:35:59,283 --> 00:36:00,784
I'm learning a lot from her.

595
00:36:02,035 --> 00:36:03,912
Well, aren't you a smooth talker?

596
00:36:03,996 --> 00:36:07,332
I could talk all night
about the reasons I fell for her.

597
00:36:13,380 --> 00:36:15,090
-Okay, all fixed.
-Already?

598
00:36:15,757 --> 00:36:17,634
If it was this simple,
why did my husband…

599
00:36:18,886 --> 00:36:20,178
Oh my, what's this?

600
00:36:22,139 --> 00:36:23,932
I figured you like flowers.

601
00:36:30,522 --> 00:36:31,523
Mr. Kang, I'm…

602
00:36:32,691 --> 00:36:33,734
Mom.

603
00:36:33,817 --> 00:36:35,694
So you've been meeting here
behind my back?

604
00:36:36,945 --> 00:36:38,655
No, you've got it all wrong.

605
00:36:38,739 --> 00:36:40,198
I ran into Ji-yoon on my way here.

606
00:36:43,493 --> 00:36:45,412
Look, I got the bungeoppang you like.

607
00:36:45,495 --> 00:36:46,872
Is it made of peas?

608
00:36:48,206 --> 00:36:50,083
Because I see
two peas in a pod right here.

609
00:36:52,878 --> 00:36:54,087
Right.

610
00:36:54,171 --> 00:36:57,090
Though I suppose a major corporation
beats a tiny corner store.

611
00:36:59,259 --> 00:37:01,720
Working at SAEUM is the one thing
I like about you.

612
00:37:03,680 --> 00:37:05,057
Well, about that…

613
00:37:05,140 --> 00:37:07,601
I'm planning to resign from SAEUM.

614
00:37:09,478 --> 00:37:12,606
He probably got poached to a better place.

615
00:37:12,689 --> 00:37:13,607
Right?

616
00:37:14,858 --> 00:37:16,068
I'm going to take a break

617
00:37:16,151 --> 00:37:17,903
and look for a new path.

618
00:37:17,986 --> 00:37:20,405
You threw away the one thing I liked?

619
00:37:20,489 --> 00:37:21,823
Forget it.

620
00:37:21,907 --> 00:37:23,992
A divorcé, maybe.
But a funemployed man? No.

621
00:37:24,076 --> 00:37:24,952
Mom.

622
00:37:26,453 --> 00:37:27,663
-Mom, come on.
-Hey.

623
00:37:27,746 --> 00:37:28,580
Hang on.

624
00:37:29,539 --> 00:37:30,624
Mom!

625
00:37:40,217 --> 00:37:43,303
Hey. Why'd you bring that up
when things were going well?

626
00:37:43,387 --> 00:37:45,514
She would've been angrier
if she found out later.

627
00:37:45,597 --> 00:37:47,975
Good grief, you really are frustrating.

628
00:37:48,684 --> 00:37:50,936
I thought a lot about how to convince you,

629
00:37:52,771 --> 00:37:54,314
but it boiled down to one thing.

630
00:37:54,982 --> 00:37:55,816
I…

631
00:37:57,109 --> 00:37:58,193
like him a lot.

632
00:37:59,987 --> 00:38:01,113
I really do.

633
00:38:02,614 --> 00:38:05,242
How can you trust a man
who walked out on not just his marriage

634
00:38:05,325 --> 00:38:06,618
but his career as well?

635
00:38:06,702 --> 00:38:07,911
But I do trust him.

636
00:38:08,829 --> 00:38:10,414
He's the only person

637
00:38:10,497 --> 00:38:12,791
who makes me live
most authentically as myself.

638
00:38:13,709 --> 00:38:17,254
So I know he'll find a job
that lets him live as his true self too.

639
00:38:19,214 --> 00:38:21,591
Even his personality is just your dad's.

640
00:38:22,926 --> 00:38:24,636
There's nothing I like about him.

641
00:38:25,595 --> 00:38:27,764
I guess I take after you a lot, Mom.

642
00:38:28,432 --> 00:38:29,850
Take after me? No way.

643
00:38:31,810 --> 00:38:34,646
You're far smarter
and more upstanding than me.

644
00:38:38,066 --> 00:38:39,651
You're my greatest pride.

645
00:38:42,779 --> 00:38:45,240
I'm sorry, Mom.

646
00:38:54,207 --> 00:38:58,003
You could say
we crossed a major hurdle, no?

647
00:38:59,004 --> 00:39:00,505
How did you reach that conclusion?

648
00:39:01,423 --> 00:39:03,633
She said, "A divorcé, maybe."
Remember?

649
00:39:04,217 --> 00:39:06,053
That means she's softening up on you.

650
00:39:06,136 --> 00:39:08,096
She also said, "But a funemployed? No."

651
00:39:08,180 --> 00:39:11,475
Well, that's only a temporary problem.

652
00:39:13,185 --> 00:39:14,603
It might take a while.

653
00:39:16,313 --> 00:39:17,898
Then I'll just have to provide for you.

654
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:23,070
Tomorrow will be my last day at work.

655
00:39:26,448 --> 00:39:28,075
-Tomorrow?
-Yes.

656
00:39:28,784 --> 00:39:31,453
I'll hand in the paperwork
and use my remaining paid leave.

657
00:39:33,038 --> 00:39:35,123
So the final day is really here.

658
00:39:35,749 --> 00:39:38,168
You'll still root for me
as a colleague, right?

659
00:39:39,419 --> 00:39:40,337
It's a pity,

660
00:39:41,213 --> 00:39:42,047
but yes.

661
00:39:51,223 --> 00:39:53,975
LETTER OF RESIGNATION
NAME: KANG SI-WOO

662
00:39:55,894 --> 00:39:57,270
It feels like a waste

663
00:39:57,354 --> 00:39:59,856
to throw away
everything you've worked for,

664
00:40:00,816 --> 00:40:02,109
and everything that would've followed.

665
00:40:02,734 --> 00:40:03,777
Think it over again.

666
00:40:03,860 --> 00:40:06,488
I can't work like I do now
under any other boss.

667
00:40:06,571 --> 00:40:08,031
Can't you just

668
00:40:08,115 --> 00:40:10,283
stay on as our boss, Mr. Kang?

669
00:40:18,083 --> 00:40:19,918
CONFIRM SUBMISSION
SEND DOCUMENT?

670
00:40:20,001 --> 00:40:20,836
CONFIRM

671
00:40:20,919 --> 00:40:22,462
DOCUMENT SENT

672
00:40:36,059 --> 00:40:38,061
I take it Mr. Noh botched his assignment.

673
00:40:38,145 --> 00:40:39,813
You made him do it knowing he would.

674
00:40:43,108 --> 00:40:44,693
If I couldn't convince you to stay,

675
00:40:45,569 --> 00:40:47,112
I at least had to make them liable.

676
00:40:47,195 --> 00:40:49,781
Which is why you played the card
that I was a key asset.

677
00:40:49,865 --> 00:40:51,032
Exactly.

678
00:40:52,284 --> 00:40:53,618
It's not too late to change your mind.

679
00:40:53,702 --> 00:40:54,703
No.

680
00:40:55,370 --> 00:40:58,081
I won't be able to give you the support
you expect from me.

681
00:40:59,583 --> 00:41:00,458
Instead…

682
00:41:05,297 --> 00:41:06,131
What's this?

683
00:41:06,798 --> 00:41:08,008
You'll find this useful.

684
00:41:08,675 --> 00:41:10,760
Here's what you asked for the other day.

685
00:41:12,095 --> 00:41:13,346
Your hunch was spot on.

686
00:41:13,430 --> 00:41:16,933
Subcontractors have been wining and dining
Mr. Noh and Mr. Ko on golf trips

687
00:41:17,017 --> 00:41:19,644
in exchange for securing contracts
to sell their products.

688
00:41:19,728 --> 00:41:21,855
Those two were boasting
as if they were about to

689
00:41:21,938 --> 00:41:23,231
take over Home-AI soon.

690
00:41:24,524 --> 00:41:25,942
This shows the expenses
those vendors paid.

691
00:41:29,946 --> 00:41:30,780
Thanks.

692
00:41:31,615 --> 00:41:33,909
It looked like your Vice President
was involved too.

693
00:41:33,992 --> 00:41:34,826
You sure about this?

694
00:41:37,621 --> 00:41:38,788
Yeah.

695
00:41:38,872 --> 00:41:40,207
It's just the vendors' words now,

696
00:41:40,290 --> 00:41:42,876
so you'll need
a proper investigation to prove it.

697
00:41:43,752 --> 00:41:46,254
How you play this card
is entirely up to you.

698
00:41:52,260 --> 00:41:54,429
So you're leaving me a bomb
as a parting gift.

699
00:41:56,890 --> 00:41:59,768
There's no point
in trying to make you stay, right?

700
00:42:00,560 --> 00:42:01,394
You're right, ma'am.

701
00:42:02,771 --> 00:42:04,356
I made it this far thanks to you.

702
00:42:06,816 --> 00:42:08,568
You got here on your own merit.

703
00:42:08,652 --> 00:42:09,486
I look forward

704
00:42:10,070 --> 00:42:11,571
to seeing Kang Si-woo's next chapter.

705
00:42:12,614 --> 00:42:13,573
Thank you.

706
00:42:17,160 --> 00:42:19,955
This is a non-compete agreement.

707
00:42:21,331 --> 00:42:22,916
It states you can't work

708
00:42:22,999 --> 00:42:25,252
in the same industry
for a year after leaving here.

709
00:42:27,963 --> 00:42:28,964
Okay.

710
00:42:33,468 --> 00:42:36,054
What the heck? I haven't even
approved his resignation yet!

711
00:42:36,137 --> 00:42:37,639
The President approved it.

712
00:42:37,722 --> 00:42:38,640
What?

713
00:42:38,723 --> 00:42:41,601
We were told to skip the exit interview
and wrap this up quickly.

714
00:42:47,482 --> 00:42:52,696
KANG SI-WOO

715
00:42:57,617 --> 00:42:59,286
Thank you for everything.

716
00:42:59,369 --> 00:43:00,370
Thank you.

717
00:43:00,954 --> 00:43:02,247
I'll sign off now.

718
00:43:02,330 --> 00:43:05,834
SAEUM
KANG SI-WOO, MANAGER

719
00:43:17,220 --> 00:43:18,096
Mr. Kang!

720
00:43:19,556 --> 00:43:22,058
Ms. Cha is in the product showroom and…

721
00:43:23,893 --> 00:43:25,020
Mr. Kang!

722
00:43:31,943 --> 00:43:32,944
Why are you here so early?

723
00:43:33,778 --> 00:43:34,696
Gosh, he's super fast!

724
00:43:34,779 --> 00:43:37,532
You were supposed to bring him here
right on time, you dummy.

725
00:43:37,615 --> 00:43:38,742
I mean,

726
00:43:38,825 --> 00:43:41,411
I was literally just trying to say
Ms. Cha was waiting

727
00:43:41,494 --> 00:43:42,912
in the product showroom,

728
00:43:43,580 --> 00:43:45,915
but he bolted
before I could even finish my sentence!

729
00:43:45,999 --> 00:43:49,002
What, did you think
she was in some kind of trouble?

730
00:43:49,711 --> 00:43:52,464
I've never seen
the great Kang Si-woo run that hard.

731
00:43:54,299 --> 00:43:56,509
What is everyone doing here?

732
00:43:56,593 --> 00:43:58,553
They're tearing down this place soon,

733
00:43:58,636 --> 00:44:01,097
so Mr. Kim here suggested
we run one final test.

734
00:44:01,181 --> 00:44:02,182
Test?

735
00:44:02,265 --> 00:44:04,142
You can't quit
until we do a final inspection

736
00:44:04,225 --> 00:44:06,436
to see if the product
we launched runs perfectly!

737
00:44:07,937 --> 00:44:09,064
It's ready.

738
00:44:14,277 --> 00:44:15,653
That's right.

739
00:44:16,529 --> 00:44:20,909
This was the exact moment
you were supposed to bring him in

740
00:44:20,992 --> 00:44:22,160
so that we could do this!

741
00:44:23,995 --> 00:44:26,664
-Congrats on your resignation!
-Congrats on your resignation!

742
00:44:27,248 --> 00:44:28,500
Congratulations.

743
00:44:30,335 --> 00:44:32,504
We couldn't let you leave
without a farewell party.

744
00:44:32,796 --> 00:44:34,422
How could you, Mr. Kang?

745
00:44:34,923 --> 00:44:37,717
I was the last one to find out again.

746
00:44:39,761 --> 00:44:40,637
I'm sorry.

747
00:44:46,684 --> 00:44:48,770
Sir, did you just apologize with a smile?

748
00:44:49,479 --> 00:44:50,480
Then "No sorry" is over,

749
00:44:50,563 --> 00:44:51,940
and "No smile" is over too.

750
00:44:52,023 --> 00:44:54,442
And look, "No people" is over too.

751
00:44:54,526 --> 00:44:56,528
That means you're no longer Three-No-Man.

752
00:44:58,279 --> 00:44:59,114
Right.

753
00:44:59,948 --> 00:45:02,033
Now that I'm leaving,

754
00:45:02,951 --> 00:45:05,245
I finally see the reason
I could have stayed.

755
00:45:06,663 --> 00:45:09,958
Only today did I learn
what makes work worthwhile for me.

756
00:45:11,126 --> 00:45:13,795
You were my reason,
and you made it worthwhile.

757
00:45:14,796 --> 00:45:15,922
Thank you all

758
00:45:17,173 --> 00:45:18,133
for everything.

759
00:45:32,063 --> 00:45:33,606
All right, then.

760
00:45:34,649 --> 00:45:36,276
-Ta-da!
-Wow!

761
00:45:36,901 --> 00:45:39,112
You can't have a farewell party
without a toast.

762
00:45:39,988 --> 00:45:41,281
Here, let me pour you a drink.

763
00:45:46,161 --> 00:45:48,455
You're Kang Si-woo after all.
You'll do great anywhere.

764
00:45:49,622 --> 00:45:50,457
Thank you.

765
00:45:51,249 --> 00:45:52,083
Here.

766
00:45:52,625 --> 00:45:56,254
The office is going to feel so empty
once Ms. Yoon leaves too.

767
00:45:57,714 --> 00:45:59,048
I'll be back before you know it.

768
00:45:59,132 --> 00:46:00,008
Sure.

769
00:46:05,305 --> 00:46:06,347
Just a little for me.

770
00:46:10,852 --> 00:46:12,353
Did everyone get a drink?

771
00:46:12,437 --> 00:46:14,898
Now, Sr. Associate Jeon.
Give us a killer toast.

772
00:46:14,981 --> 00:46:15,857
Yes, well…

773
00:46:17,108 --> 00:46:20,528
Mr. Kang, wherever you go, I hope…

774
00:46:21,654 --> 00:46:24,616
your notorious reputation continues.

775
00:46:25,450 --> 00:46:26,534
Now, everybody.

776
00:46:26,618 --> 00:46:28,495
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

777
00:46:28,578 --> 00:46:30,580
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

778
00:47:23,007 --> 00:47:26,135
NO SCHEDULE TODAY

779
00:47:45,863 --> 00:47:46,781
I'm sorry, ma'am.

780
00:47:47,615 --> 00:47:50,702
So you're saying
you sent out that half-baked report

781
00:47:51,536 --> 00:47:54,455
and actually CC'd
the managing director too?

782
00:47:55,582 --> 00:47:56,708
I thought I had to.

783
00:48:00,003 --> 00:48:02,130
I'm pretty sure I sent you

784
00:48:02,213 --> 00:48:04,048
a detailed guide on email etiquette.

785
00:48:04,465 --> 00:48:05,300
I'm sorry.

786
00:48:06,259 --> 00:48:07,302
I haven't memorized it yet.

787
00:48:08,845 --> 00:48:09,679
Drink this.

788
00:48:12,974 --> 00:48:16,060
Chamomile is supposed to be great
when you're tense and nervous.

789
00:48:24,819 --> 00:48:25,820
Thank you.

790
00:48:27,238 --> 00:48:28,364
One time,

791
00:48:29,282 --> 00:48:31,451
I accidentally dropped a zero

792
00:48:31,993 --> 00:48:34,621
from every number
in a profit-and-loss simulation.

793
00:48:35,997 --> 00:48:39,125
That means 10,000 won became 1,000 won.

794
00:48:39,917 --> 00:48:42,503
Wow, you must've gotten an earful.

795
00:48:43,129 --> 00:48:44,088
What was it he said?

796
00:48:45,548 --> 00:48:47,634
"One mistake is enough."

797
00:48:47,717 --> 00:48:49,636
Repeated mistakes aren't mistakes anymore.

798
00:48:49,719 --> 00:48:51,346
They show the person's incompetence.

799
00:48:52,388 --> 00:48:54,557
I'm disappointed in you, Ms. Cha.

800
00:48:57,560 --> 00:48:59,020
Just hearing that gives me chills.

801
00:49:00,688 --> 00:49:01,773
But still,

802
00:49:03,149 --> 00:49:05,485
I genuinely learned so much
from that person.

803
00:49:09,906 --> 00:49:12,575
He taught me what it truly means
to be a teammate.

804
00:49:13,368 --> 00:49:14,619
It must be true

805
00:49:15,620 --> 00:49:16,621
if you say so.

806
00:49:18,122 --> 00:49:19,374
He taught me…

807
00:49:21,626 --> 00:49:24,128
how to put my own well-being first.

808
00:49:24,212 --> 00:49:26,130
So I told you to cut back
on the instant food,

809
00:49:26,214 --> 00:49:28,216
sweet coffee, and sugary drinks!

810
00:49:30,176 --> 00:49:31,969
He told me to screw sacrifice plays…

811
00:49:34,263 --> 00:49:36,057
and be the hero instead.

812
00:49:43,106 --> 00:49:44,607
He showed me

813
00:49:46,150 --> 00:49:48,653
how to fight back
against unfair treatment.

814
00:49:48,736 --> 00:49:49,654
Also,

815
00:49:50,238 --> 00:49:53,241
that word has more weight
the less you use it.

816
00:49:54,450 --> 00:49:56,327
Don't say "sorry" when you're with me.

817
00:49:56,911 --> 00:49:57,912
Especially at work.

818
00:49:58,788 --> 00:50:00,331
He taught me…

819
00:50:02,709 --> 00:50:04,168
everything I need to know.

820
00:50:14,387 --> 00:50:16,347
What's wrong, all of a sudden?

821
00:50:58,681 --> 00:50:59,599
Welcome back.

822
00:51:00,224 --> 00:51:01,184
Come have some tea.

823
00:51:01,684 --> 00:51:03,269
Did you have a good day today?

824
00:51:03,352 --> 00:51:04,312
Yes.

825
00:51:04,896 --> 00:51:06,564
Like you said, I did absolutely nothing

826
00:51:06,647 --> 00:51:08,149
and spent the day lazing around.

827
00:51:08,900 --> 00:51:09,776
Well done.

828
00:51:12,278 --> 00:51:13,279
Ta-da.

829
00:51:17,116 --> 00:51:18,034
What are these for?

830
00:51:18,117 --> 00:51:19,827
To celebrate you graduating from SAEUM.

831
00:51:20,620 --> 00:51:22,455
Thank you for all your hard work.

832
00:51:22,538 --> 00:51:25,124
You were the best boss
I've ever had, Mr. Kang.

833
00:51:30,505 --> 00:51:31,506
Thank you.

834
00:51:32,548 --> 00:51:35,176
Then can I also graduate
from being called "Mr. Kang"?

835
00:51:36,135 --> 00:51:36,969
Sorry?

836
00:51:37,428 --> 00:51:38,596
I'm not your boss anymore.

837
00:51:39,597 --> 00:51:40,431
Right.

838
00:51:41,390 --> 00:51:42,225
Then…

839
00:51:43,518 --> 00:51:44,352
Si-woo.

840
00:51:45,728 --> 00:51:46,771
Yeah, Ji-yoon.

841
00:51:49,357 --> 00:51:50,399
Put your mug down.

842
00:51:51,150 --> 00:51:51,984
Why?

843
00:51:52,068 --> 00:51:53,653
You'll end up spilling otherwise.

844
00:52:30,898 --> 00:52:31,732
Do you remember

845
00:52:33,317 --> 00:52:36,779
eating like this right here
on our very first date?

846
00:52:37,363 --> 00:52:38,322
I do.

847
00:52:39,574 --> 00:52:42,952
I brought a fancy bottle of wine,
and you got us sundae.

848
00:52:43,953 --> 00:52:46,789
Who could've guessed
you'd bring wine in those days?

849
00:52:47,832 --> 00:52:50,334
A drink back then always meant soju.

850
00:52:52,670 --> 00:52:55,882
You dragged out fixing that radio
for days just to make a move on me,

851
00:52:56,465 --> 00:52:58,676
to set up a drinking date
under the pretext of apologizing.

852
00:52:59,760 --> 00:53:01,846
So I thought
it was going to be a romantic evening.

853
00:53:01,929 --> 00:53:02,847
Still,

854
00:53:03,723 --> 00:53:06,767
wine and sundae
went surprisingly well together, right?

855
00:53:09,478 --> 00:53:12,565
And I thought Ji-yoon and that guy
would make a good pairing too.

856
00:53:13,858 --> 00:53:16,277
Let the kids figure out their own lives.

857
00:53:16,986 --> 00:53:17,904
And…

858
00:53:19,071 --> 00:53:20,823
let's focus on our lives instead.

859
00:53:22,742 --> 00:53:24,327
We can just graduate from marriage.

860
00:53:31,542 --> 00:53:33,377
If you want that so badly,

861
00:53:34,378 --> 00:53:35,212
then go ahead.

862
00:53:42,219 --> 00:53:43,471
But marry me again.

863
00:53:47,350 --> 00:53:49,268
When the time comes and you pass away,

864
00:53:51,562 --> 00:53:52,980
I don't want you to be alone.

865
00:53:56,817 --> 00:53:58,694
I'll spend the rest of my days making up

866
00:53:59,820 --> 00:54:01,489
for what I didn't do for you in the past.

867
00:54:05,534 --> 00:54:06,744
So let me stay by your side…

868
00:54:08,913 --> 00:54:10,039
on your final day.

869
00:54:14,126 --> 00:54:15,127
Are you seriously

870
00:54:16,504 --> 00:54:18,255
using my deathbed as a pick-up line?

871
00:54:20,424 --> 00:54:21,509
A pick-up line?

872
00:54:31,435 --> 00:54:32,269
Hye-gyeong.

873
00:54:35,272 --> 00:54:36,273
Forget everything else.

874
00:54:39,193 --> 00:54:40,194
I just want to

875
00:54:40,945 --> 00:54:42,279
outlive you by exactly one day.

876
00:54:45,157 --> 00:54:48,119
Oh, stop it, Cha Yeong-mook.

877
00:54:50,830 --> 00:54:51,789
I'm sorry.

878
00:54:53,165 --> 00:54:54,834
Forgive me, won't you?

879
00:55:05,803 --> 00:55:08,639
How come you're here alone?
You said you'd come with your sister.

880
00:55:09,598 --> 00:55:12,309
That was the plan,
but she went to see her boyfriend.

881
00:55:13,894 --> 00:55:16,105
Well, if she has a boyfriend,
he takes priority.

882
00:55:16,188 --> 00:55:17,106
Exactly.

883
00:55:18,107 --> 00:55:19,483
Boyfriend over family, I guess.

884
00:55:21,318 --> 00:55:22,361
Are you done with interviews?

885
00:55:22,945 --> 00:55:25,197
I can lend you this place
whenever you need.

886
00:55:27,199 --> 00:55:29,660
I haven't settled on my next piece yet.

887
00:55:30,286 --> 00:55:31,829
What kind of story do you want to tell?

888
00:55:31,912 --> 00:55:32,788
This time…

889
00:55:33,789 --> 00:55:35,958
instead of people just dating at work,

890
00:55:36,042 --> 00:55:38,169
I want to write something where people

891
00:55:38,252 --> 00:55:40,629
give 100 percent to both work and love.

892
00:55:42,214 --> 00:55:44,216
Work emergencies happen left and right,

893
00:55:45,259 --> 00:55:46,635
and their love lives are a mess,

894
00:55:46,719 --> 00:55:49,597
so they cry and throw fits and all that,

895
00:55:50,514 --> 00:55:52,475
but they still clock in tomorrow.

896
00:55:54,935 --> 00:55:55,936
So, a horror story?

897
00:55:56,812 --> 00:55:58,105
Office workers won't read that.

898
00:55:58,189 --> 00:55:59,899
That's exactly my dilemma.

899
00:56:01,650 --> 00:56:05,279
Should I stick to something that sells
instead of what I want to write?

900
00:56:08,199 --> 00:56:09,450
"404 FOUND."

901
00:56:10,159 --> 00:56:12,369
You know how you sometimes see

902
00:56:13,120 --> 00:56:15,790
"404 NOT FOUND"
when you browse on the Internet?

903
00:56:16,457 --> 00:56:19,126
That means the server itself
is still running,

904
00:56:19,210 --> 00:56:21,253
but there's no corresponding webpage.

905
00:56:21,337 --> 00:56:22,755
Which means "I exist,

906
00:56:23,547 --> 00:56:25,007
but I can't find the answer."

907
00:56:25,633 --> 00:56:26,509
The thing is,

908
00:56:26,592 --> 00:56:29,261
a 404 isn't a fatal system error.

909
00:56:29,345 --> 00:56:32,056
If you take a little break and reboot it,

910
00:56:33,557 --> 00:56:34,809
you might find it again.

911
00:56:35,351 --> 00:56:38,646
So you're saying
I should come here, grab a drink,

912
00:56:38,729 --> 00:56:40,731
and unwind when I get writer's block?

913
00:56:40,815 --> 00:56:42,149
Bingo.

914
00:56:42,233 --> 00:56:44,568
Oh, man. I totally fell for it.

915
00:56:45,694 --> 00:56:47,404
-Pour me another one.
-With pleasure.

916
00:56:54,328 --> 00:56:57,164
You always come here to clear your head
when you're stuck anyway.

917
00:57:00,668 --> 00:57:01,627
I'm going to spend my time

918
00:57:02,461 --> 00:57:05,005
traveling with my wife from now on,

919
00:57:05,714 --> 00:57:07,633
so come fix things
and look after the store.

920
00:57:10,511 --> 00:57:13,722
Take your time and figure out
what you want to do while you're at it.

921
00:57:21,230 --> 00:57:23,983
Stop worrying about me
and just take care of yourself, Da-ra.

922
00:57:24,859 --> 00:57:26,902
Don't live on burgers, okay?

923
00:57:27,820 --> 00:57:29,572
And don't get hurt playing futsal.

924
00:57:30,781 --> 00:57:32,867
All right, I'll call when I land.

925
00:57:39,456 --> 00:57:42,168
MON AMOUR JAE-IN

926
00:57:47,464 --> 00:57:50,134
This caller is unavailable.
You'll be redirected to voicemail.

927
00:57:52,553 --> 00:57:54,305
Why isn't he picking up?

928
00:58:08,944 --> 00:58:11,447
MON AMOUR JAE-IN

929
00:58:12,239 --> 00:58:13,073
Hey, Jae-in.

930
00:58:14,241 --> 00:58:15,075
No-ah.

931
00:58:31,884 --> 00:58:33,510
What are you doing here?

932
00:58:35,137 --> 00:58:36,347
I couldn't let you go alone.

933
00:58:42,061 --> 00:58:43,020
I'll escort you there.

934
00:58:43,520 --> 00:58:44,939
Jae-in.

935
00:58:51,987 --> 00:58:54,990
I never expected our first trip together
would be to Senegal.

936
00:58:55,074 --> 00:58:57,117
I love it. It's perfect.

937
00:59:03,707 --> 00:59:04,667
Thank you.

938
00:59:04,750 --> 00:59:05,709
Don't mention it.

939
00:59:18,514 --> 00:59:19,932
Working late again tonight?

940
00:59:22,017 --> 00:59:24,061
Nope, this is me slacking off.

941
00:59:24,144 --> 00:59:27,231
You make it sound like
you're working on a plastic model kit.

942
00:59:27,314 --> 00:59:28,148
Did you have dinner?

943
00:59:29,108 --> 00:59:29,942
I'm unemployed, so…

944
00:59:30,901 --> 00:59:32,653
-What about lunch?
-I had ramyeon.

945
00:59:32,736 --> 00:59:35,239
Your quality of life
has seriously tanked since you quit.

946
00:59:35,906 --> 00:59:39,326
I recall you saying that health was
the one thing you'd never compromise on.

947
00:59:41,120 --> 00:59:43,872
I'll be fine
since I have a naggy person by my side.

948
00:59:54,341 --> 00:59:55,217
It's delicious.

949
00:59:55,301 --> 00:59:56,552
How's your work going?

950
00:59:56,635 --> 00:59:57,928
I've got the basic blueprint.

951
01:00:00,097 --> 01:00:01,307
What about you?

952
01:00:01,390 --> 01:00:04,184
The rookie is driving me nuts
with a new crisis every day.

953
01:00:04,268 --> 01:00:05,894
I don't want to go to work tomorrow.

954
01:00:07,062 --> 01:00:10,024
Then why don't you play hooky
and hang out here with me?

955
01:00:10,733 --> 01:00:11,567
Should I?

956
01:00:12,735 --> 01:00:14,153
Do you mind if I join you?

957
01:00:14,236 --> 01:00:15,362
Unwind this first.

958
01:00:23,537 --> 01:00:24,496
Next…

959
01:00:26,790 --> 01:00:28,459
we detach this part.

960
01:00:28,959 --> 01:00:30,461
-Then…
-Look at that!

961
01:00:31,295 --> 01:00:34,048
Even your detaching technique
is on another level.

962
01:00:34,131 --> 01:00:35,007
Try this one too.

963
01:01:11,710 --> 01:01:12,544
Take a seat.

964
01:01:12,628 --> 01:01:14,421
What did you work on today?

965
01:01:14,505 --> 01:01:16,632
Well, I refined this idea.

966
01:01:23,472 --> 01:01:25,599
Please look for an office space
around Seongwol-dong.

967
01:01:26,642 --> 01:01:27,935
It doesn't have to be that big.

968
01:01:30,813 --> 01:01:32,689
Have a look. I'll carry you like this.

969
01:01:35,192 --> 01:01:36,110
You know what?

970
01:01:43,325 --> 01:01:46,829
6 MONTHS LATER

971
01:01:56,463 --> 01:01:59,675
Automotive audio is fundamentally
a battle against noise.

972
01:01:59,758 --> 01:02:02,094
You have to suppress
engine hum, road noise,

973
01:02:02,177 --> 01:02:04,096
and even the sound of the wind.

974
01:02:07,933 --> 01:02:09,893
MARKET STATUS QUO
AND IDENTIFYING ISSUES

975
01:02:13,564 --> 01:02:14,815
It's not just about noise,

976
01:02:14,898 --> 01:02:17,985
it's about controlling it
after reading the driver's emotions.

977
01:02:18,902 --> 01:02:20,070
What do you think, Toto?

978
01:02:20,821 --> 01:02:23,490
If I speak up, you're going to dump
all the work on me again.

979
01:02:24,032 --> 01:02:26,869
Well, you happen to be
the most hardworking teammate we have.

980
01:02:26,952 --> 01:02:28,537
Stop gaslighting me.

981
01:02:28,620 --> 01:02:30,664
Keep this up,
and I'm taking a leave.

982
01:02:33,667 --> 01:02:34,543
Manager Cha!

983
01:02:42,718 --> 01:02:43,552
SAEUM
CHA JI-YOON, MANAGER

984
01:02:43,635 --> 01:02:44,511
Ms. Cha!

985
01:03:01,361 --> 01:03:02,488
Has everyone eaten?

986
01:03:02,571 --> 01:03:04,072
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes, ma'am.

987
01:03:04,156 --> 01:03:06,450
Okay, then. Let's officially
kick off the first meeting

988
01:03:06,533 --> 01:03:08,702
of the newly revived
Future Household Appliances Task Force.

989
01:03:12,206 --> 01:03:13,373
Babe!

990
01:03:20,255 --> 01:03:21,840
What brings you all the way out here?

991
01:03:21,924 --> 01:03:23,842
I'm here to brave
the rush-hour subway with you.

992
01:03:26,470 --> 01:03:28,263
Then let's walk a bit first.

993
01:03:28,347 --> 01:03:30,140
It'll be super packed if we get on now.

994
01:03:31,099 --> 01:03:32,059
Okay, then.

995
01:03:42,402 --> 01:03:45,239
We can't do this, we can't do that.

996
01:03:45,322 --> 01:03:48,784
If they keep shooting down everything,
what can we even make?

997
01:03:48,867 --> 01:03:51,995
At this rate,
we're going to lose everything

998
01:03:52,079 --> 01:03:53,372
to our competi--

999
01:04:10,264 --> 01:04:12,057
A fall like that
can break a bone, you know.

1000
01:04:22,943 --> 01:04:24,278
We should get married

1001
01:04:24,361 --> 01:04:26,196
before we get any older, Ji-yoon.

1002
01:04:29,283 --> 01:04:30,117
Wow.

1003
01:04:31,201 --> 01:04:32,911
It's an actual ring this time.

1004
01:04:33,579 --> 01:04:34,997
So say yes, will you?

1005
01:04:39,293 --> 01:04:40,127
Sorry.

1006
01:04:41,461 --> 01:04:42,296
Again?

1007
01:04:43,046 --> 01:04:44,464
This time…

1008
01:04:52,431 --> 01:04:53,724
I want to propose to you.

1009
01:04:57,936 --> 01:05:00,939
But I'm a bit slammed
with work these days.

1010
01:05:01,607 --> 01:05:03,150
Can I put it on you after this project?

1011
01:05:03,984 --> 01:05:06,028
At this rate, we'll be getting
matching hearing aids instead.

1012
01:05:15,454 --> 01:05:17,414
I don't know
when the wedding will be, but…

1013
01:05:23,462 --> 01:05:25,047
It'll be with me

1014
01:05:25,130 --> 01:05:26,465
on one spring day.

1015
01:05:41,021 --> 01:05:42,314
I love being in love.

1016
01:05:43,857 --> 01:05:45,984
It makes everything seem possible.

1017
01:05:49,529 --> 01:05:51,573
Let's grab some fried chicken
and beer nearby.

1018
01:05:51,657 --> 01:05:53,116
Again? Aren't you sick of it?

1019
01:05:53,200 --> 01:05:55,786
How could I ever
get sick of chicken and beer?

1020
01:05:57,537 --> 01:05:59,081
Even when there's no map to follow,

1021
01:05:59,164 --> 01:06:00,624
even when we get lost for a while,

1022
01:06:01,792 --> 01:06:03,960
the one thing that helps us find the way…

1023
01:06:04,044 --> 01:06:05,170
In the end,

1024
01:06:05,796 --> 01:06:06,755
it's love.

1025
01:06:09,049 --> 01:06:10,592
I'm staying over at your place tonight.

1026
01:06:11,843 --> 01:06:13,679
My new apartment is freezing.

1027
01:06:14,388 --> 01:06:16,056
Don't you have to clock in tomorrow?

1028
01:06:16,556 --> 01:06:17,391
Yeah.

1029
01:06:18,141 --> 01:06:20,060
Going to work
doesn't mean I can't be in love.

1030
01:06:27,442 --> 01:06:28,318
I love you.

1031
01:06:30,362 --> 01:06:31,196
I love you too.

1032
01:06:35,575 --> 01:06:37,244
-I love being in love.
-I love being in love.

1033
01:06:54,886 --> 01:07:00,183
GREAT JOB TODAY

1034
01:07:00,267 --> 01:07:07,232
I WILL SIGN OFF NOW

1035
01:07:07,315 --> 01:07:10,235
SPECIAL THANKS TO BAE YU-RAM
AND PARK SEO-HAM

1036
01:08:16,092 --> 01:08:18,094
Subtitle: Yenny Kang
